# AI Engineering Lab — operating system

This repo is a **learning laboratory**, not an encyclopedia and not a dump of tutorials.

**Current gate:** read `99-META/GATE-STATUS.md` first. While `owner_policy` is standing auto-advance through Gate 10, start the next gate only after **QA chair PASS** — not after a human named-gate message. Human-in-the-loop is off until that policy is cleared.

Authoritative spec: `AI_Engineering_Knowledge_Repository_Master_Prompt.md`. Agent entrypoint: `AGENTS.md`.

## Mission

Take an experienced cloud/data engineer from logical understanding → implementation → engineering → production → architect judgment → principal-level trade-offs. Cover **all major agent flavors**, not only RAG. Explicitly teach when an agent is the wrong solution.

## Non-negotiables

- Do not generate the full curriculum in one pass.
- Do not create empty markdown files. Content only when it is meaningful.
- Do not invent APIs, SDKs, cloud SKUs, pricing, or performance numbers. Mark `UNVERIFIED`.
- Prefer local durable artifacts over repeated LLM/web calls.
- Bridge from Python/SQL/Spark/Kafka/Databricks/cloud — do not reteach basic programming.
- Markdown is the authoring source; HTML is generated (`app/tools/render-pages.py`). Do not dual-write.

If the user says "continue" without naming a gate **and** standing auto-advance is unset, ask which gate. If standing auto-advance is set, continue the factory at the current gate after QA PASS.
